      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "while I also want them VERY badly (oh the possibilities, I could make bumper cars as an avatar). we mostly just have to wait for them to finish. based on the bit we do know the avatar dynamics are tied to the new physics engine. so they have to complete both of those before they can give us one or the other (or else things might have to get rewritten because of how they interact, which would likely break some avatars).\nAlso keep this in mind, game dev normally you take the expected completion time (including setbacks) and add 50-70% onto itself (things always take longer than planned). \nIf I remember right the original video in april said sometime late summer, so about 5 months would be nearing the end of summer as they said. Add 50-70% onto 5 months and you get between 7.5 and 8.5 months, which lands you a range of the later half of December and the early half January (AKA soon). So I'd say just wait about a month and a half and see what happens.  If there's still nothing, then yeah... something likely got caught on something and it'll be a long while.\nLook at it this way, at least its not \"The Last Guardian\". That game was announced in 2009 and was delayed so much it released in 2016 almost 2017 XD (it was originally planned for 2011. delayed a whole 5 years, and it was 7 since it was announced). AKA, things could always be WAY worse.",
